From 43208eea7d97be02a94a695b1197c19dd20d83be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:30:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mediacodec: 3D MVC with the hardware MVC decoder
 (libmvc3dplay mvc3d_hw)

With libmvc3dplay 2026.10.18 and the mvc3d kernel module 2026.10.18, a 3D
MVC stream shown in 3D (or with --mediacodec-mvc-hw=2 also in 2D) is decoded
by the legacy Amlogic MVC decoder instead of MediaCodec + the software
decoder: libmvc3dplay rewrites frame_num against the decoder's wrap-around
artefacts, mvc3d composes the pictures (frame packed or the base view) and a
video tunnel shown by the video surface's sideband stream displays them.

The legacy decoder excludes MediaCodec, so the decoder restarts with an
mc_api of its own (MvcHw_*): queue_in feeds the library, dequeue_out gives
its pictures (display order, pts from the library), release_out_ts queues a
picture into the tunnel at its time; the output thread, the opaque pictures,
flush and drain stay as they are. When the hardware decoder does not start
(busy, old module) the decoder goes back to MediaCodec and 3D to the software
path. --mediacodec-mvc-hw: 0 software, 1 hardware (default), 2 hardware also
in 2D.

Message-Id: <20261018-dvfel-mediacodec-mvc3d-hw@djnice>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
